Article 5: For the purposes of these Provisions, "real name" refers to the name used on the identification documents that conform to laws, administrative regulations, and relevant state provisions.
The following identification documents are real-name certificates:
(1) For Chinese citizens residing within the territory, the resident identity card or temporary resident identity card;
(2) For Chinese citizens under the age of 16 residing within the territory, the household register;
(3) For members of the Chinese People's Liberation Army, the military identification document; for members of the Chinese People's Armed Police, the armed police identification document;
(4) For residents of Hong Kong and Macao, the entry permit for traveling between Hong Kong/Macao and the mainland; for residents of Taiwan, the travel permit for traveling between Taiwan and the mainland or other valid travel documents;
(5) For foreign citizens, the passport.
Matters not specified in the preceding paragraph shall be handled in accordance with relevant laws, administrative regulations, and relevant state provisions.
